\paragraph{Loss Function Isolation.}
Training BCE with identical Gumbel-Sigmoid sampling and Lagrangian enforcement yields PPL 38.02 (best of 3 LR sweeps), worse than vanilla BCE (27.97): the Lagrangian penalty interferes with per-neuron optimization when the loss cannot coordinate neurons globally. % exp_id: bce_gumbel_lagrangian_isolation
The loss function's effect ($\Delta$PPL=26.23) is $6.6\times$ larger than the relaxation method's ($\Delta$PPL=3.98), confirming distribution-level supervision as the decisive factor.
